<h3>Patios and Outdoor Living Spaces</h3>
<p>Outdoor living areas should feel comfortable and functional. Layering several light sources, such as downlights, string lights, accent lights, step lights and wall fixtures, usually works best. The goal is a space that feels inviting rather than overly bright. Explore ideas on our <a href="/services/patio-outdoor-living-lighting/">patio and outdoor living lighting</a> page.</p>

<h3>Pools and Water Features</h3>
<p>Water interacts beautifully with light; reflections add movement that few other landscape elements can match. Popular applications include pool perimeter lighting, waterfalls, ponds and fountain accents. See <a href="/services/pool-water-feature-lighting/">pool and water feature lighting</a>.</p>

